synthesis:
## Verdict

Proposal 3 has the highest total, 18, against 15 for proposal 1 and 14 for proposal 2. It supplies the base:
- native disclosure semantics;
- an untouched `createSection` function;
- section rules that keep the 8 px landing;
- one test seam for every Contents click;
- a landing that compares against a predicted set of differences.

The synthesis swaps its in-flow drawer for proposal 1's overlay panel. An index in flow at the top of the page cannot be reached once the reader scrolls past the first screen, and that is the problem the user named. The overlay needs proposal 2's paint isolation. That isolation also fixes the header overpaint present at 9fb2be1.

## Shell

The shell lives in `app/browser/factories.ts`. `createShell` changes in five places:
1. **Body row.** `row g-5` becomes `row gx-5`. The 3rem horizontal gutter stays, so the main column keeps its width at 390 and 1280 px. Under lg, the empty Contents column no longer adds a vertical gutter.
2. **Contents region.** `section#contents.col-lg-3[aria-label="Contents"]` holds one `div#contents-panel` with the classes `offcanvas-lg offcanvas-start sticky-lg-top vh-100 overflow-y-auto px-4 px-lg-0 py-3`. That panel wraps the single `createContents` nav, and the `d-lg-none` copy is deleted. The panel is the chrome's only `.sticky-lg-top` element and comes first in document order, so `#offset` writes the same two inline properties:
   - under lg, `top` and `max-height` put the fixed drawer at the header's bottom and stop it at the viewport bottom;
   - from lg, they bound the sticky sidebar as at 9fb2be1.
3. **Header toggle.** After the Color mode group, the controls wrapper gains a `details.d-lg-none.ms-auto` element. It holds a `summary.btn.btn-sm.btn-outline-secondary.text-body-emphasis` reading `Contents`, with `aria-controls="contents-panel"`.
4. **Brand.** The `Bootstrap 5.3.8` span gains `d-md-none d-lg-inline`. The `light-390` journal (`tmp/journey/light-390.txt`) records the Stylesheets group at 353.3 px and Light plus Dark at 104.2 px. With the brand and the toggle added, the 768 px row comes within a few pixels of the 744 px bar. That sum uses my estimates for the brand and toggle widths, not a run. The span stays in the DOM, so `factories.test.ts:842` holds.
5. **Rhythm.** In the members map, every section except its group's last gains `pb-4 border-bottom`, and the group `h2` adds `border-primary`. A chapter rule therefore reads stronger than a section rule. No section gets top padding.

`createContents` changes its grid to `row row-cols-2 row-cols-lg-1 g-3 gx-lg-0`.

## Why the toggle is a `summary`

I ruled for a `summary` element over proposal 1's `a.btn` link, for these reasons:
- It reads as role `button` through `readRole` (`IMPLICIT_ROLES.SUMMARY`).
- It states collapsed or expanded natively through `readStates`.
- It activates on both Enter and Space.
- `clickDisclosure` drives it, with the reachability filter.
- It is not a `button` element. Every `header button` reader, and `getByRole('button')`, still finds exactly the five choices. `#select` ignores it, because `closest('button')` returns null.
- `.btn` sets `display: inline-block` from the `bootstrap` layer. In both Tailwind compiles that layer sorts after preflight's `base` layer (the recipe.json layer order reads `reset, base, bootstrap, …`), so no face draws a disclosure marker.

The link form is refused: Space does not activate a link, and a link that does not navigate misstates its role.

## Drawer behavior

`app/browser/Showcase.ts` gains `#fold(open)`. It sets `details.open`, toggles the registry class `show` on the panel, and swaps `text-body-emphasis` for `active` on the summary. Every listener carries the mount's signal. Bootstrap's `.offcanvas-lg` rules (`dist/src/bootstrap/index.css`:6377-6436) supply the rest: under lg the panel is fixed, hidden and translated, `show` slides it in, and reduced motion removes the transition. From lg none of those rules apply.

The drawer folds at once on any of these routes:
- a click on a panel link, with the default hash navigation left to run;
- Escape, which also focuses the summary;
- `focusout` to an element outside both the panel and the summary;
- a document click outside both;
- `#offset` finding that the panel's computed `position` is no longer `fixed`.

Opening leaves focus on the summary. The panel comes next in DOM order, so Tab reaches `Containers`. There is no focus trap, `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal` or backdrop, so J8 still reads `countDialogs()` as 0 and `collectOverlays()` as empty. The engine never binds the panel, because it has no `.offcanvas` class and no `data-bs-*` attribute.

## Paint isolation

Paint isolation lands first. `z-0` goes on every specimen card body whose descendants resolve a z-index of 3 or more at rest, as long as the card holds no live dropdown, modal or offcanvas. That follows the existing stage convention at engine-states.html:125, offcanvas.html:158 and modal.html:192. Without it:
- frozen tooltips and popovers paint over the 1045 drawer and can block J3's `userEvent.click` at 390;
- the z-3 panels and the sticky specimens paint over the header.

## Native slot

The Native group's slot is `{ id: 'native', title: 'Native surfaces' }`, placed between `interactions` and `tailwindcss`. Because the group sits before Tailwind, `collectBootstrapGroups` and the variant expectation pick it up from `GROUPS` with no edit, and J1's `TAILWIND Tailwind on Bootstrap markup` reading holds.

The group lands with the first stage B demo, B4, and never empty:
- the variant case expects a `group-ID` heading for every group (integration.test.ts:1152-1156);
- `heads every group` counts one `main > div` per group (factories.test.ts:890).

In that landing, the census `LIVE_GROUP` becomes a set holding `interactions` and `native`. Each Native section is a pair row (`row row-cols-1 row-cols-xl-2 g-4`):
- a `Default` figure and an `Opt-in` figure, both `figure.card.flex-fill.mb-0` inside `col d-flex`;
- a caption badge after each title;
- opener names that carry the variant, so no existing `COMPONENT_TABLES` row resolves them, and the group's own tables.

`main.ts` keeps `createBootstrapPlugins()`, so stage B's prediction that no existing table row moves still holds. This round writes the convention into the guide only.

## Tests

`tests/setupBrowser.ts` gains two helpers:
- `openContents()` does nothing from lg or when the drawer is already open. Otherwise it calls `clickDisclosure('Contents')` and waits for the first Contents link to render.
- `clickContents(name)` calls `openContents()` and then clicks the named link.

The seven click sites, J1, J2, J3, the variant case, the contrast and offset cases, and the population reading all go through these helpers. The population reading and the contrast case run at the 414 px default viewport, which is under lg.

At 390, J2's path becomes: skip link, the five buttons, `['button', 'Contents']`, Enter, `Containers`, then Escape back to the folded summary.

`STATES` gains `contents-drawer`, making 77 states. The added drawer case covers:
- the fold routes;
- a Tab after a pick landing inside the target region;
- every Contents link hit-testing to itself while the drawer is open over the Tooltips and Popovers sections.

## Landing

The landing compares a baseline journey run at the branch tip with a candidate run. It accepts only these differences:
- the `signature coverage` rows at light-1280 and light-390;
- the preservation `excluded` field;
- the J1 and J2 Journal entries at 390;
- J3's `minimum heading margin`;
- the banner and Contents trees;
- the 77 states.

Any contrast, engine, Tailwind-reading or `390 header` difference refuses the landing. Land this round before B3. B4 lands the Native group.

## Deferred

Each of these waits for the user's first visual check:
- proposal 1's current-section marker;
- proposal 2's caption chips, anchor chips, `thead.small` and `tbody.table-group-divider`;
- a scroll lock, which needs an inline style on `body`.

## Corrections to the brief

The brief needs four corrections:
- there are seven Contents click sites, not four;
- the default viewport for the `app:browser` and `setup:browser` suites is 414 px, which is under lg;
- the checkout is at 9fb2be1, not ab7a8e7;
- the 768 px header row has almost no slack.

